            <div xml:id="d919">

                <pb facs="1103" n="993" xml:id="pg993"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.5122/40</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-05-19">May 19, 1931</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 494</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department has received your despatch
                    No. 932 of April 11, 1931, in regard to the collection of a house tax from
                    American citizens at Tsinan.</p>
                <p>The action taken by the American Consul at Tsinan, as stated in your despatch
                    under acknowledgment, is approved.</p>
                <p>Very truly yours,</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State:<lb/><signed>W. R. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Castle, Jr.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
